---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /
---
{% from "icons.njk" import icon %}
{%- set categories = collections.content | childrenOf("/") -%}

<section class="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <img class="hero__logo" src="/assets/img/logo.svg" width="168" height="168"
         alt="{{ site.name }} logo: a leaf threaded by a data pipeline, orbited by a satellite" />
    <h1>{{ site.title }}</h1>
    <p class="hero__lead">
      Build, automate, and validate satellite-driven carbon accounting and
      <abbr title="Measurement, Reporting, Verification">MRV</abbr> systems —
      from raw imagery to audit-ready emissions inventories.
    </p>
    <div class="hero__cta">
      {%- for cat in categories -%}
        {%- set slug = cat.url | topSlug -%}
        {%- set meta = site.sections[slug] -%}
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="{{ site.url }}{{ cat.url }}">
          {{ icon(meta.icon if meta else "layers") }}
          <span>{{ meta.label if meta else cat.data.title }}</span>
          {{ icon("arrow-right") }}
        </a>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head">
      <h2>A technical resource for spatial MRV automation</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-intro">
      <p>
        Modern carbon accounting has moved from spreadsheets into distributed,
        spatially explicit data pipelines. <strong>{{ site.name }}</strong> is a
        practitioner-focused resource for engineering those pipelines: deterministic
        geospatial processing, rigorous uncertainty quantification, and
        cryptographically verifiable audit trails that meet institutional standards.
      </p>
      <p>
        Written for ESG engineers, climate data scientists, and Python GIS teams, every
        guide pairs production-ready code with the compliance context behind it — GHG
        Protocol scoping, ISO 14064, CSRD, and the registry workflows that turn satellite
        observations into defensible inventories.
      </p>
      <p>
        The library is organized into four sections covering the full lifecycle:
        designing MRV architecture, processing satellite imagery for emissions tracking,
        modeling and validating carbon stocks, and orchestrating and governing the
        pipelines that tie them together — schema contracts, workflow orchestration, and
        registry standards. Pick a section below to dive in.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head">
      <h2>Explore the content</h2>
      <p>Four sections, each with focused topics and step-by-step Python implementation guides.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      {%- for cat in categories -%}
        {%- set slug = cat.url | topSlug -%}
        {%- set meta = site.sections[slug] -%}
        {%- set topics = collections.content | childrenOf(cat.url) -%}
        <article class="card card--rich">
          <span class="card__icon">{{ icon(meta.icon if meta else "layers") }}</span>
          <h3><a href="{{ site.url }}{{ cat.url }}">{{ meta.label if meta else cat.data.title }}</a></h3>
          <p>{{ meta.blurb if meta else cat.data.description }}</p>
          {%- if topics | length -%}
            <ul class="topic-links">
              {%- for t in topics -%}
                <li><a href="{{ site.url }}{{ t.url }}">{{ icon("chevron-right") }}<span>{{ t.data.title }}</span></a></li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}
          <a class="card__more" href="{{ site.url }}{{ cat.url }}">Browse this section {{ icon("arrow-right") }}</a>
        </article>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
